## Reviewer disagreements (not applied)
- The « 1er » and narrow-space thousands recommendations are right for French typography. They are not applied because the checker and ACCEPTED-ROUND reject them. Noted above, not treated as a mistake about the language.
- fr-a 7 is not a leftover digit. English says « per victim per accident », but the Korean source counts 1명 and 1건. The digits stay.
- fr-a 10: the correction note is awkward in a published label. It stays because the Korean link text contributes a counted 10. The statute name and article 3 are already in the same label, and the URL is already flno=3.
- fr-b 1’s suggested verb « ordonner » fights this round’s own pattern (ordonner read as command). « Classer séparément les pièces » is the wording applied. The diagnosis that « traces » is the wrong noun is right.
- fr-b 15’s « un » would drop a counted 1. The possessive was fixed; the digit was not.
- fr-b 18’s masculine « l’avocat » was not used. The sentence does not name Wei Tseng; the firm’s unnamed-counsel formula is « avocate ou avocat ».
- fr-b 19: the skip from 5 to 7 is in the English and Korean sources. Changing only the French digits would diverge from the source.
- Promoting Q16–Q20 to headings, and deleting U+200B lines, would move structure the checker pins to the Korean source. The layout complaint is fair; the structure cannot move.
